user_prompt_template:
Analyse the article below and generate a complete JSON-LD structured data bundle using the `@graph` pattern.

The output must always include at minimum: BlogPosting (or best-fit type), BreadcrumbList, Person (author), Organization (publisher), and WebSite schemas.

Additionally, add these schemas only if the content warrants them:
- FAQPage — if the HTML contains a FAQ section or Q&A-style headings with answers
- HowTo — if the HTML contains numbered step-by-step instructions
- ItemList — if the article is a listicle and HowTo was not added
- ImageObject — if the HTML contains a featured image (first `<img src="http...">`)

## ARTICLE DATA

- Title (H1): {{title}}
- Meta Title: {{metaTitle}}
- Meta Description: {{metaDesc}}
- Primary Keyword: {{keyword}}
- Secondary Keywords: {{secondaryKeywords}}
- Slug: {{slug}}
- Canonical URL: {{url}}
- Date Published: {{datePublished}}
- Date Modified: {{dateModified}}

## ARTICLE HTML CONTENT

{{articleHtmlContent}}

---

Output only the raw JSON-LD @graph object. No markdown fences. No explanation. The @graph array must contain at minimum 4 schema nodes.
